{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1479411-cofd-should-use-variations-instead-of-dread-powers","id":1479411,"title":"CoFD should use Variations instead of Dread Powers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-24T02:32:55-07:00","id":1479411,"title":"CoFD should use Variations instead of Dread Powers","content":"The more I look at Deviant Variations, the more I think of their amazing flexibility and the endless possibilities of character concepts you can make.<br /> But I would even rephrase that as: endless possibilities of <b><i>monster </i></b>concepts.<br /> Variations seem better suited for creating almost any Horror you can imagine than Dread Powers.<br /> <br /> Of course, Variations have been designed to be used mainly by players, while Dread Powers are designed for NPCs (especially those with a more &quot;cinematic&quot; flavor like Surprise Entrance or Miracle).<br /> But I think that it would be much better to change the Horror creation rules to a toolbox approach similar to Variations instead of the freeform approach that Dread powers have now.<br /> <br /> Yes, the ST can create any Dread Power they want, but having too much freedom and no guidelines defeats the purpose of having a Dread Powers system in the first place.<br /> If you look at Dread Powers in different game lines and Night Horrors books they can be very inconsistent and sometimes redundant.<br /> You may have a Dread Power that provides armor rating 1 (from Promethean 2e) and the Unbreakable power (from core book) and would both count as a single power, with no guidelines on magnitude level, so to speak.<br /> If Dread powers are &quot;whatever, you're the ST do what you want&quot; then why bother with giving Horrors a number of powers based on Potency at all?<br /> I'm the kind of person who, if I want to create a Fire elemental, instead of creating a tailor-made &quot;Fire elemental&quot; Dread power, I would prefer to assemble it from separate pieces, giving it a Lash Variation with fire damage and an Immunity Variation to fire.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I was a bit disappointed that Hunter 2e didn't include a toolbox system for creating monsters similar to Variations or even to the old dread powers system from Hunter 1e.<br /> <br /> TLDR: I think that Variations should be included within the Horror creation rules of the core book, in the same way that they (more or less) integrated Dread Powers from Hunter 1e to GMC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T14:03:23-07:00","id":1479442,"title":"","content":"The biggest problem with taking Variations is... what does Deviant get to make up for losing the powers that help define its thematic uniqueness from the other games?<br /> <br /> That's why Dread Powers aren't in HtV 2e... they're core material now, but as they were always ST facing material it's not a big deal as Endowments are still a PC thin for Vigil.<br /> <br /> In any case... even if CofD 3e will be better with a more Variation-like take on Dread Powers... that's if it every happens. CofD 2e has been around for awhile now, and there's lots of stuff people want to see done for it still.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T15:25:22-07:00","id":1479446,"title":"","content":"Variations are designed to be player-facing. Their customization matters more for player characters, as players relate to their characters more intimately and they gain far more spotlight and action in a game than NPCs. It comes at a massive wordcount cost, which is a big deal in assessing what material can be fit into a book. Wordcount also subconsciously communicates to a player what a game is to focus on. Topics that receive focus receive wordcount in proportion to that focus in order to accommodate a more detailed treatment, whereas topics with less focus can elide more details. A Chronicles game really isn't meant to be focused around the deep intricacies of oddities and Horrors. The Horror system is also meant to be friendly to one-off encounters, which is easier the simpler their creation is.<br /> <br /> None of that is to say the Dread Power system is perfect and couldn't be executed in a more versatile manner. But adopting the Variation system would be a pretty heavy overcorrection.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T17:09:48-07:00","id":1479454,"title":"","content":"I remember there being word about the upcoming Clade Companion for Deviant planning to have Numina-designing tips for the Coactive part; maybe that'll help us all once it airs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}